What is Hydrogen Gas?
Hydrogen Gas (H2) is the lightest and most abundant element in the universe. It is a colorless, odorless, tasteless, and highly flammable gas. Hydrogen is not a direct energy source like fossil fuels but an energy carrier that stores and delivers energy in a usable form. It is primarily produced through steam methane reforming (gray hydrogen), electrolysis of water (green hydrogen), or gasification of coal (brown hydrogen).

